<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch10-what-integrals-measure">
  <title>What Integrals Measure</title>
  <shorttitle>Applications of Integration</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>To set up an integral for a total quantity, identify the contribution of a small piece and add those contributions over the relevant interval. For volume, the contribution is cross-sectional area times thickness. For mass, it is density times length or area. This chapter develops that approach for geometric quantities, work, fluid force, averages, and probability, with units used to check each formula.</p></introduction>

